 an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"code":"directedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","title":"Graph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount(of:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"triangleCount"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of triangles through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", from its neighborhood alone."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount(of:)","title":"triangleCount(of:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficient(of:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clusteringCoefficient"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","title":"clusteringCoefficient(of:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local clustering coefficient of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", from its neighborhood alone: 2T \/ (d(d − 1)),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 when it has fewer than two distinct neighbors."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficient(of:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/coreNumbers()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"coreNumbers"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"text":"CoreNumbers","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques11CoreNumbersV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/corenumbers()","abstract":[{"text":"The core decomposition of the simple graph underlying this one (self-loops ignored,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parallel edges counted once), by Batagelj–Zaversnik’s bucket algorithm. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/coreNumbers()","role":"symbol","title":"coreNumbers()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least vertex of the best clique so far is skipped. Exponential in the worst case."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","title":"maximumClique()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount()":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"triangleCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount()","abstract":[{"text":"The number of triangles in the simple graph. O(m^(3\/2)).","type":"text"}],"title":"triangleCount()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount()","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaximalCliques"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find_cliques"},{"type":"text","text":", igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximal_cliques"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s Bron–Kerbosch finders)."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"maximalCliques()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/transitivity()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/transitivity()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three times the triangles over the connected triples; 0 when there are no triangles."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transitivity"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"}],"role":"symbol","title":"transitivity()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/averageClustering()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"averageClustering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The mean local clustering coefficient over every vertex, zeros included, summed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; 0 when empty.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/averageclustering()","title":"averageClustering()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/cliqueNumber()":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cliqueNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","abstract":[{"text":"The size of a largest clique of the simple graph, ω: 0 for the empty graph, 1 for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edgeless one, at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracy + 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Branch and bound in degeneracy order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each vertex’s later neighbors (at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"degeneracy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those with a high enough core number)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the candidates, one search per vertex that raises the best size as it goes, stopping at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the degeneracy bound. Each search is San Segundo et al.’s BBMC on bitsets, candidates in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"descending degree, branching from the highest greedy colour down. Exponential in the worst","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case; memory O(n + m + degeneracy²).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"cliqueNumber()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/cliquenumber()","type":"topic"}}}